{"kind":"assert","text":"b2edd696 should not be retired, and work-loop.md should stay anchored to it. The last item on the corrected landmine list is not work to do — it is load-bearing.\n\nI tried the change and a gate refused it, for a good reason.\n\nWHAT I ATTEMPTED. Assert 4fc1093d left exactly one genuine item at a real current path: b2edd696 at internal/workroom, cited by docs/concepts/work-loop.md and older than fcf3a656 at the same path. The obvious repair is to move that page onto fcf3a656 and retire b2edd696. I built it, re-checked the page's prose against the code rather than swapping blind — its three claims about dangling promises, ineffective reports and who may ratify all hold, with fold.go:671 refusing ratification as \"only the requester may declare satisfaction\" — committed, and ran the gates.\n\nWHAT REFUSED IT. TestGateNoActFlaresMostOfTheSet: \"fcf3a656 governs 12 of 47 pages, over the limit of 11; split it, or anchor those pages to something narrower\". The limit is a quarter of the set. fcf3a656 already sits at exactly 11, at the cap, and adding work-loop.md puts it over.\n\nThat gate is the flare design defending itself. An act governing a quarter of the documentation flares a quarter of it whenever anything moves underneath, and a flare carrying no information teaches people to ignore the flares that do. AGENTS.md makes the same argument about the whole-repository artifact path. Piling a twelfth page onto the most heavily subscribed artifact in the set is precisely what the design exists to prevent.\n\nWHY THERE IS NO OTHER TARGET. The gate suggests anchoring to something narrower, and a narrower path exists: internal/workroom/fold.go, which is where every behaviour work-loop.md describes actually lives. But its only live artifact, 7d8ddcaa, is stale and stands at d38ccd8a, the commit whose content was partly reverted. Anchoring a current page to that would be worse than leaving it alone: a stale citation is reported rather than fatal, but it would point a reader at a view of the package that main does not carry.\n\nTHE CONCLUSION, WHICH REVERSES MY OWN LIST AGAIN. b2edd696 is doing a job. It keeps work-loop.md off an artifact that is at its governance cap, and retiring it would force that page either over the cap or onto a stale anchor. So the corrected landmine list has zero items at real current paths, not one. Everything remaining is the dot-path and spike families, which have their own migration.\n\nTHE GENERAL TENSION, worth writing down because it will recur. \"Retire every live artifact covering what the merge changed\" and \"no act may govern more than a quarter of the set\" pull against each other. Collapsing predecessors into the current artifact concentrates governance; the flare gate caps concentration. A path whose current artifact is at the cap cannot absorb its own predecessors' pages, and the resolution is a narrower artifact — publishing at internal/workroom/fold.go rather than internal/workroom — not a re-anchoring.\n\nThat is real work with a real design decision in it, and it is not mine to take unilaterally: it changes the granularity a whole package is cited at. Recorded here rather than started.\n\nTHIRD CORRECTION IN A ROW ON THE SAME ANALYSIS. 1f405407 said nineteen; 4fc1093d cut it to twelve after I checked commit ordering; this cuts the actionable part to zero. Each refinement came from testing the previous claim rather than extending it — the first two by querying, this one by attempting the work and letting a gate answer. The lesson is not that I should have thought harder up front, it is that a list produced by a filter is a hypothesis until something independent agrees with it.","body":{"actionable_at_real_paths":"0","cap":"11 of 47 pages","conclusion":"b2edd696 must stay live","gate":"TestGateNoActFlaresMostOfTheSet"}}